  "details": "VRC Creator Companion SDK version: v2.3.3\n\nHello! I've been having some issues with the SDK lately. \n\nWhenever I create a new project everything seems fine, until i decide to uplaod it. At first, it will be stuck with the blue \"Avatar built\" bar for an hour from what i've witnessed (Seen on image), or it will either give me an error after at least 10 minutes of waiting, and then my entire SDK breaks, deleting the info of my avatar and not letting me click anything at all (seen on image). And when i try to re-open the proyect of an avatar that's been already uploaded on my account, the information on the SDK will never load no matter how long i wait.\n\nI already re installed the Creator Companion, Unity, and even VRC on Steam, but aparently it only functions correctly at very late night, almost around 3am MST.  That has been the only times where it properly lets me upload any type of avatars. only past midnight. \n\nI'm not sure if this is a server issue, or an SDK issue in general, but I am hoping to get this solved soon. I will be providing screen shots of my situation and error messages I get.\n\nThank you.",
